        <p>The Examiner, Saturday, February 15, 1908.</p>
        <p>of the latter lived with Jones, who cohabited. with Gorman since the death of his wife in June of last year. The man's average wages for the last four years were 355. Mr. Knowles described how the children had been neglected, and the filthy condition of their bodies, clothing and bedding.—An inspector of the National Society for the Prevention of Cruelty to Children corroborated, and said the couple had spent the money ; in drink. Gorman was sent to prison for four months with hard labnur, and Jones for two months without ! hqr d labour.</p>
