        <p>Services for Sunday. Wycliffe Church, Be%sey-street : Morning 10.30 and evening 0.30, Rev. J. Yonge.—ln the evening a special servite for young people will be held, followed by a social hour in the Memorial Hall. Bold-street Wesleyan Church : Morning 10.30, Rev. W. Mellor ; evening 6.30, Rev. T. Miller. Bewsey-road Wesleyan Church : Morning 10.30, Rev T. Miller ; evening 6.30, Rev. S. Pitt. Evening sub- ject : "Character and circumstances; or a good servant and a bad master."</p>
        <p>A SUGGESTION.</p>
        <p>The Chairman said he had noticed in the reports of the shooting competitions that one or two men appeared to take the prizes in the monthly events, and he thought a system of handicapping might be introduced. He thought if something was done in that direction that it would encourage other members who were not such proficient shots. (Hear, hear.) Mr. Fletcher said he appreciated the suggestion, but they would be restricting their entries. After further discussion the matter was referred to the committee.</p>
